      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "State the principle of conservation of momentum.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "part_stem": "A firework is initially stationary. It explodes into three fragments A, B and C that move in a horizontal plane, as shown in the view from above in Fig. 3.1. Fragment A has a mass of $3m$ and moves away from the explosion at a speed of $4.0\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$. Fragment B has a mass of $2m$ and moves away from the explosion at a speed of $6.0\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ at right angles to the direction of A. Fragment C has a mass of $m$ and moves away from the explosion at a speed $v$ and at an angle $\\theta$ as shown in Fig. 3.1. Calculate:",
      "text": "the angle $\\theta$",
      "marks": 3,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "the speed $v$.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "part_stem": "The firework in (b) contains a chemical that has mass $5.0\\,\\mathrm{g}$ and has chemical energy per unit mass $700\\,\\mathrm{J\\,kg^{-1}}$. When the firework explodes, all of the chemical energy is transferred to the kinetic energy of fragments A, B and C.",
      "text": "Show that the total chemical energy in the firework is $3.5\\,\\mathrm{J}$.",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Calculate the mass $m$.",
      "marks": 3,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "M1",
          "text": "(total momentum) before = sum / total momentum after (of a system of objects) is constant"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "(no external) force / for an isolated system"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "marks": 3,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "conservation of momentum in x-direction, e.g. $3m \\times 4.0 = mv \\sin\\theta$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "conservation of momentum in y-direction, e.g. $2m \\times 6.0 = mv \\cos\\theta$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$\\tan\\theta = 1$ or $\\theta = 45^{\\circ}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$mv\\sin\\theta = 12m$ or $mv\\cos\\theta = 12m$ or $mv \\times 6)^{2}$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$v = 17\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$0.0050 \\times 700 = 3.5\\,(\\mathrm{J})$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "marks": 3,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "total kinetic energy $= \\frac{1}{2}(3m)(4.0)^{2} + \\frac{1}{2}(2m)(6.0)^{2} + \\frac{1}{2}mv^{2} = 3.5\\,(\\mathrm{J})$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$204m = 3.5$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$m = 0.017\\,\\mathrm{kg}$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
